Ordre zero: code Fokker-Planck
\layout Standard

Comme il a ete montre, l'equation de Fokker-Planck peut etre exprimee sous
 une forme totalement matricielle, sous la forme symbolique implicite 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
 &  & r_{l+1/2}p_{i+1/2}^{2}\frac{f_{i+1/2,j+1/2,l+1/2}^{\left(0\right)\left(k+1\right)}-f_{i+1/2,j+1/2,l+1/2}^{\left(0\right)\left(k\right)}}{\Delta t}\\
 &  & =-r_{l+1/2}\sum_{i^{\prime}=i-1}^{i^{\prime}=i+1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=j-1}^{j^{\prime}=j+1}\overline{\overline{M}}_{p,i^{\prime}+1/2,j^{\prime}+1/2,l+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}f_{i^{\prime}+1/2,j^{\prime}+1/2,l+1/2}^{\left(0\right)\left(k+1\right)}\\
 &  & -p_{i+1/2}^{2}\sum_{l^{\prime}=l-1}^{l^{\prime}=l+1}\overline{\overline{M}}_{r,,i+1/2,j+1/2,l^{\prime}+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}f_{i+1/2,j+1/2,l^{\prime}+1/2}^{\left(0\right)\left(k+1\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

En ordonnant les valeurs discretes de la distribution 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{i+1/2,j+1/2,l+1/2}^{\left(0\right)\left(k+1\right)}$
\end_inset 

 sous la forme d'un vecteur 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{X}$
\end_inset 

 selon la regle d'une suite 
\begin_inset Formula $\left[l\rightarrow\left\{ 0,n_{r}-1\right\} ,i\rightarrow\left\{ 0,n_{p}-1\right\} ,j\rightarrow\left\{ 0,n_{\xi}-1\right\} \right],$
\end_inset 

 on obtient une matrice diagonale 
\begin_inset Formula $\overline{\overline{\mathbf{M}}}$
\end_inset 

 par bandes,
\layout Standard

Methode implicite complete 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left(\overline{\overline{\mathbf{M}}}+\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{I}}}}{\Delta t}\right)\cdot\mathbf{X}^{\left(k+1\right)}\mathbf{=}\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{I}}}}{\Delta t}\cdot\mathbf{X}^{\left(k\right)}-\mathbf{B}^{\left(k\right)}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

Methode Cranck-Nicholson 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left(\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{M}}}}{2}+\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{I}}}}{\Delta t}\right)\mathbf{X}^{\left(k+1\right)}\mathbf{=\left(-\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{M}}}}{2}+\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{I}}}}{\Delta t}\right)X}^{\left(k\right)}-\mathbf{B}^{\left(k\right)}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula \[
\overline{\overline{\mathbf{M}}}=\overline{\overline{\mathbf{L}}}\cdot\overline{\overline{\mathbf{U}}}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula \[
\mathbf{\Delta}^{\left(k+1\right)}\mathbf{=X}^{\left(k+1\right)}-\mathbf{X}^{\left(k\right)}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula \[
\mathbf{R}^{\left(k\right)}\mathbf{=}\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{I}}}}{\Delta t}\cdot\mathbf{X}^{\left(k\right)}-\mathbf{B}^{\left(k\right)}-\left(\overline{\overline{\mathbf{M}}}+\frac{\overline{\overline{\mathbf{I}}}}{\Delta t}\right)\cdot\mathbf{X}^{\left(k\right)}=-\overline{\overline{\mathbf{T}}}\mathbf{\cdot X}^{\left(k\right)}-\mathbf{B}^{\left(k\right)}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula \[
\overline{\overline{\mathbf{L}}}\cdot\overline{\overline{\mathbf{U}}}\cdot\mathbf{\Delta}^{\left(k+1\right)}=\]

\end_inset 


